=== layout: two-panels

# Genetic Control of Sex in Drosophila

@left

- X chromosomes relative to autosome sets control _sex-lethal_ (_Sxl_).
- This master control gene switches the sex-determination pathway on or off.

@right

![Slide image 3](assets/lect06e-x_linked_genes_2/image_003.jpg)

=== layout: two-panels

# Fly sex determination: X-to-autosome ratio

@left

- [*X*]{underline=true}: X chromosome.
- [*A*]{underline=true}: one autosome set.
- Ratio 1: female.
- Ratio 0.5: male.
- Between 0.5 and 1: [*intersex*]{color=purple underline=true}.

@right

| Formula | X:A | Outcome |
| --- | --- | --- |
| X:AA | 0.5 | Male |
| XX:AAA | 0.67 | Intersex |
| XX:AA | 1 | Female |
| X:A | 1 | Initially female; dies |

=== layout: two-panels

# Fly sex determination: extended ratios

@left

- [*X*]{underline=true}: X chromosome.
- [*A*]{underline=true}: one autosome set.
- 0.5: male; 1: female.
- 0.5 < X:A < 1: [*intersex*]{color=purple underline=true}.
- X:A > 1: [*metafemale*]{color=orange underline=true}.
- X:A < 0.5: [*metamale*]{color=green underline=true}.

@right

| Formula | Ratio | Outcome |
| --- | --- | --- |
| X:AAA | 0.33 | Metamale; low viability |
| X:AA | 0.5 | Male |
| XX:AAA | 0.67 | Intersex |
| X:A | 1 | Initially female; dies |
| XX:AA | 1 | Female |
| XXX:AA | 1.5 | Metafemale; low viability |

=== layout: two-panels
@replaceme

# Summary of Sex Determination in Fruit Flies

@left

![Slide image 4](assets/lect06e-x_linked_genes_2/image_004.png)

@right

- [*metafemale*]{color=red underline=true} (or superfemale) is a low viability Drosophila with a female phenotype [(X\:A ratio > 1)]{color=red}
- [*metamale*]{color=blue underline=true} (or supermale) is a low viability Drosophila with a male phenotype [(X\:A ratio < ½)]{color=blue}
- [*intersex*]{color=purple underline=true}: intermediate sexual development in this fruit-fly X:A model (½ < X\:A ratio < 1)


